{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Without a store, a tracker keeps its records in memory only. A tracker given a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker(store:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") appends each record to it as the tracker’s worker reaches the record, before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"publishing it, and starts its records with the ones the store kept from earlier runs.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore"},{"text":" is the store this module ships: a directory of append-only segment files, bounded at 5 MiB unless you pass another ","type":"text"},{"code":"byteBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A segment is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deleted once every record in it is delivered.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A store keeps only the event types you list in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":", which conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":". Each record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a CBOR (RFC 8949) map, its event a map of its properties under their names, written through the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventMacros"},{"type":"text","text":", part of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":") writes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the conformance, and Swift’s synthesized one works too. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" writes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"type":"text","text":" property, and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"date in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Date]"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Date?]"},{"type":"text","text":", as the seconds since 2001 it stores, so it reads back exactly. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"type":"text","text":" written through the CBOR package’s own form, in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" type of your own or in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"synthesized conformance, reads back to within a rounding of a microsecond’s scale. Events of other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"types are delivered in this run but never written."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A store doesn’t read the records Traffluent 0.0.44 or earlier wrote, in an earlier format:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":" deletes their segments and reports each as a corruption."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each drop is reported on ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports"},{"text":" as a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"},{"text":": the oldest segments","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deleted to stay under the bound, a write that failed, and records recovery couldn’t read or found","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at another ","type":"text"},{"code":"schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A record whose delivery had started when the app ended comes back with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" set. Call ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()"},{"text":", after the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app moves to the background, so the records written so far survive power loss too.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An app on Apple platforms that already keeps a GRDB database can keep its records in a table of it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRDBPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","    var seats: Int = 1","}","","let store = try SegmentStore(events: [SignedUp.self], directory: directory, byteBound: 1024 * 1024)","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\", seats: 3))"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what the store writes, its bounds and recovery, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers which changes to an event’s type its stored records can be read through."}]}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"Persistence","externalID":"Persistence","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}],"role":"collection","symbolKind":"module"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Stores","anchor":"Stores","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/changingevents":{"type":"link","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","title":"Changing Events","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Changing Events","type":"text"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"events","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [any (","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events5EventP","text":"Event","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s7Codablea","text":"Codable","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":").Type], ","kind":"text"},{"text":"directory","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13SystemPackage8FilePathV","text":"FilePath","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"byteBound","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"segmentByteCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence17SegmentStoreErrorO","text":"SegmentStoreError","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/init(events:directory:bytebound:segmentbytecount:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A store keeping events of the types "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directory"},{"type":"text","text":"; it recovers the records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already there."}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending."}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence","title":"Persistence"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/dropReports":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","abstract":[{"text":"A report of each drop, in the order they happen, from recovery onwards.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/dropreports","title":"dropReports","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS","text":"AsyncStream","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence10DropReportO","text":"DropReport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DropReport","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"DropReport","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DropReport","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport","abstract":[{"text":"Records a store dropped before they were delivered, and why.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/RecordStore":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"RecordStore","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where a tracker keeps each record until it is delivered, so records survive the app ending."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/recordstore"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStoreError":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStoreError","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentStoreError","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"SegmentStoreError","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstoreerror","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"},{"type":"text","text":" throws: an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"argument it can’t open a store with, or the file system’s failure."}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SegmentStore","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore"},{"text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"size, until they are delivered.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/persistingrecords":{"titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Persisting Records","type":"text"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","type":"link","title":"Persisting Records"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/synchronize()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","abstract":[{"text":"Flushes every segment written since the last flush to storage (","type":"text"},{"code":"fsync","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), so it survives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"power loss.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol